hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19651","Hushaym narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Abdullah ibn Sufyan al-Thaqafi from his father, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah— and Hushaym said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, command me in Islam with a command I will not ask anyone about after you. He said: Say: I believe in Allah, then be upright. He said: I said: Then what do I guard against. He gestured to his tongue."
